concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-18 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "1 10B  Meaning of eligible"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-1-18 ;
    values:originalText "Note: Sector Schedules may add additional criteria for eligibility.  See also: • for the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 2.1 of Schedule 3; • for the energy sector—clause 2.1 of Schedule 4. (1) A CDR consumer is eligible, in relation to a particular data holder at a particular time, if, at that time: (a) the CDR consumer is either: (i) an individual who is 18 years of age or older; or (ii) a person who is not an individual; and (b) the CDR consumer is an account holder or a secondary user for an account with the data holder that is open; and (c) any additional criteria set by the relevant sector Schedule for this subrule are met. (2) A CDR consumer is also eligible, in relation to a particular data holder at a particular time, if, at that time:" ;
    skos:definition "Note: Sector Schedules may add additional criteria for eligibility.  See also: • for the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 2.1 of Schedule 3; • for the energy sector—clause 2.1 of Schedule 4. (1) A CDR consumer is eligible, in relation to a particular data holder at a particular time, if, at that time: (a) the CDR consumer is either: (i) an individual who is 18 years of age or older; or (ii) a person who is not an individual; and (b) the CDR consumer is an account holder or a secondary user for an account with the data holder that is open; and (c) any additional criteria set by the relevant sector Schedule for this subrule are met. (2) A CDR consumer is also eligible, in relation to a particular data holder at a particular time, if, at that time:"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c43b7ee8c4d493f54709d3a1a274ca37db35d8bb39146d3ae68704cdfa9c1956" ;
