concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-20 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "1 10D  Meaning of sponsorship arrangement, sponsor and affiliate"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-1-20 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A sponsorship arrangement is a written contract between a person with unrestricted accreditation (the sponsor) and another person (the affiliate), under which:   Preliminary  Part 1 Interpretation  Division 1.3 Section 1.10D Competition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020 (a) the sponsor agrees to disclose to the affiliate, in response to a consumer data request made by the affiliate in accordance with subrule 5.1B(2), CDR data that it holds as an accredited data recipient; and (b) the affiliate undertakes to provide the sponsor with such information and access to its operations as is needed for the sponsor to fulfil its obligations as a sponsor. Note: A person does not need to have sponsored accreditation to enter into a sponsorship arrangement as an affiliate, but will need it to make the consumer data requests mentioned in paragraph (a) (2) A sponsorship arrangement may also provide for the sponsor to: (a) make consumer data requests at the request of the affiliate; or (b) use or disclose CDR data at the request of the affiliate." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A sponsorship arrangement is a written contract between a person with unrestricted accreditation (the sponsor) and another person (the affiliate), under which:   Preliminary  Part 1 Interpretation  Division 1.3 Section 1.10D Competition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020 (a) the sponsor agrees to disclose to the affiliate, in response to a consumer data request made by the affiliate in accordance with subrule 5.1B(2), CDR data that it holds as an accredited data recipient; and (b) the affiliate undertakes to provide the sponsor with such information and access to its operations as is needed for the sponsor to fulfil its obligations as a sponsor. Note: A person does not need to have sponsored accreditation to enter into a sponsorship arrangement as an affiliate, but will need it to make the consumer data requests mentioned in paragraph (a) (2) A sponsorship arrangement may also provide for the sponsor to: (a) make consumer data requests at the request of the affiliate; or (b) use or disclose CDR data at the request of the affiliate."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "50018473d7943ef4c1fa3109d1589e3f48bfd7f2dedd4266655f25e1ce91e523" ;
    cof:pageNumber "36"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-20-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-1-20-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.36" .
