doc:sch-4-sec-1-38 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "1 26  Dispute resolution—primary data holders and secondary data holders" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Where a primary data holder requests relevant information from a secondary data holder in relation to a consumer complaint or dispute with the primary data holder that relates to an SR data request, the secondary data holder must provide the information to the extent that it is reasonable to do so.   Product data requests  Part 2 Application of rules in relation to SR data  Division 1.5 Section 2.1 Competition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020" ;
    cof:pageNumber "50"^^xsd:integer .

concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-2-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "2 1  Simplified outline of this Part"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-2-4 ;
    values:originalText "This Part deals with product data requests. Such requests are made using a data holder’s product data request service. A product data request may be for required product data, voluntary product data, or both. When requested in accordance with this Part, a data holder: • must, subject to an exception outlined in this Part, disclose required product data; and • may, but is not required to, disclose voluntary product data. In either case, the data is disclosed to the person who made the request, in machine-readable form and in accordance with the data standards. A data holder must not impose conditions, restrictions or limitations of any kind on the use of the disclosed data. A fee cannot be charged for the disclosure of required product data, but could be charged for the disclosure of voluntary product data." ;
    skos:definition "This Part deals with product data requests. Such requests are made using a data holder’s product data request service. A product data request may be for required product data, voluntary product data, or both. When requested in accordance with this Part, a data holder: • must, subject to an exception outlined in this Part, disclose required product data; and • may, but is not required to, disclose voluntary product data. In either case, the data is disclosed to the person who made the request, in machine-readable form and in accordance with the data standards. A data holder must not impose conditions, restrictions or limitations of any kind on the use of the disclosed data. A fee cannot be charged for the disclosure of required product data, but could be charged for the disclosure of voluntary product data."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "150b91917a319441b917637bb80cc32dc2ec4dc942918d74fe9cee082e5cf96a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "51"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Data holder must disclose required product data and may disclose voluntary product data." ;
    dc:description "required product data" ;
