doc:sch-4-sec-2-7-ss-2a a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "2(2A) 4  Disclosing product data in response to product data request" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2A) If the data holder discloses any requested voluntary product data to the requester, it must do so: (a) through its product data request service; and (b) in accordance with the data standards. Note: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "52"^^xsd:integer .

concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-2-7-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "2(3) 4  Disclosing product data in response to product data request"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-2-7-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) The data holder must, subject to subrule (4) and rule 2.5: (a) disclose the requested required product data to the requester: (i) through its product data request service; and (ii) in accordance with the data standards; and (b) include in the disclosed data any required product data that is: (i) the subject of the product data request; and (ii) contained: (A) on the data holder’s website; or (B) in a disclosure document that relates to the product. Note 1: See rule 1.7 for the meaning of “required product data”.  See also: • for the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 3.1 of Schedule 3; • for the energy sector—clause 3.1 of Schedule 4. Note 2: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8). Note 3: A fee cannot be charged for the disclosure of required product data: see section 56BU of the Act." ;
    skos:definition "(3) The data holder must, subject to subrule (4) and rule 2.5: (a) disclose the requested required product data to the requester: (i) through its product data request service; and (ii) in accordance with the data standards; and (b) include in the disclosed data any required product data that is: (i) the subject of the product data request; and (ii) contained: (A) on the data holder’s website; or (B) in a disclosure document that relates to the product. Note 1: See rule 1.7 for the meaning of “required product data”.  See also: • for the banking sector and non-bank lenders sector—clause 3.1 of Schedule 3; • for the energy sector—clause 3.1 of Schedule 4. Note 2: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8). Note 3: A fee cannot be charged for the disclosure of required product data: see section 56BU of the Act."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9a72d72700f6226746c0123f7db15abaa7fed16302b93be29c77707262738153" ;
    values:partOf concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-2-7 ;
    cof:pageNumber "52"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Data holder must disclose required product data to requester." ;
    dc:description "Yes" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
