doc:sch-4-sec-2-7-ss-6 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "2(6) 4  Disclosing product data in response to product data request" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(6) In this rule, disclosure document includes: (a) a Product Disclosure Statement within the meaning of the Corporations Act 2001; or (b) a key facts sheet within the meaning of the National Consumer Credit Protection Act 2009; or (c) a similar document that is required by law to be disclosed to a customer prior to entering into a contract with that customer." ;
    cof:pageNumber "52"^^xsd:integer .

concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-2-8 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "2 5  Refusal to disclose required product data in response to product data"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-2-8 ;
    values:originalText "request (1) Despite subrule 2.4(3), the data holder may refuse to disclose required product data in response to the request in circumstances (if any) set out in the data standards. (2) The data holder must inform the requester of such a refusal in accordance with the data standards. Civil penalty: (a) for an individual―$50,000; and (b) for a body corporate―$250,000." ;
    skos:definition "request (1) Despite subrule 2.4(3), the data holder may refuse to disclose required product data in response to the request in circumstances (if any) set out in the data standards. (2) The data holder must inform the requester of such a refusal in accordance with the data standards. Civil penalty: (a) for an individual―$50,000; and (b) for a body corporate―$250,000."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1f58b9145b24d108d7ac38887338b3ea3229833b9c1e418250343f907bfd1047" ;
    cof:pageNumber "53"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-2-8-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-2-8-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.53" .
doc:sch-4-sec-2-8 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "2 5  Refusal to disclose required product data in response to product data" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "request (1) Despite subrule 2.4(3), the data holder may refuse to disclose required product data in response to the request in circumstances (if any) set out in the data standards. (2) The data holder must inform the requester of such a refusal in accordance with the data standards. Civil penalty: (a) for an individual―$50,000; and (b) for a body corporate―$250,000." ;
    cof:pageNumber "53"^^xsd:integer .

