concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-3-8 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "3 5  Refusal to disclose required consumer data in response to consumer data"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-3-8 ;
    values:originalText "request (1) Despite subrule 3.4(3), the data holder may refuse to disclose required consumer data in response to the request: (a) if the data holder considers this to be necessary to prevent physical, psychological or financial harm or abuse; or (aa) in relation to an account that is blocked or suspended; or (b) in circumstances (if any) set out in the data standards. (2) The data holder must inform the CDR consumer of such a refusal in accordance with the data standards. Civil penalty: (a) for an individual―$50,000; and (b) for a body corporate―$250,000.   Consumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4 Preliminary  Division 4.1 Section 4.1 Competition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020" ;
    skos:definition "request (1) Despite subrule 3.4(3), the data holder may refuse to disclose required consumer data in response to the request: (a) if the data holder considers this to be necessary to prevent physical, psychological or financial harm or abuse; or (aa) in relation to an account that is blocked or suspended; or (b) in circumstances (if any) set out in the data standards. (2) The data holder must inform the CDR consumer of such a refusal in accordance with the data standards. Civil penalty: (a) for an individual―$50,000; and (b) for a body corporate―$250,000.   Consumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4 Preliminary  Division 4.1 Section 4.1 Competition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1f58b9145b24d108d7ac38887338b3ea3229833b9c1e418250343f907bfd1047" ;
    cof:pageNumber "56"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-3-8-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-3-8-ss-2 ;
