doc:sch-4-sec-4-9-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "4(3) 3  Request for accredited person to seek to collect CDR data" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) In giving the consents, the CDR consumer gives the accredited person a valid request to seek to collect that CDR data from the CDR participant. Note: If the accredited person seeks to collect CDR data under this Part without a valid request, it will contravene privacy safeguard 3 (a civil penalty provision under the Act): see section 56EF of the Act." ;
    cof:pageNumber "60"^^xsd:integer .

concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-9-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "4(4) 3  Request for accredited person to seek to collect CDR data"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-4-9-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) The request ceases to be valid if the collection consent is withdrawn. Note: So long as the use consent is not also withdrawn, the accredited person could continue to use CDR data it had already collected in order to provide the requested goods or services. However, the notification requirement of rule 4.18A would apply." ;
    skos:definition "(4) The request ceases to be valid if the collection consent is withdrawn. Note: So long as the use consent is not also withdrawn, the accredited person could continue to use CDR data it had already collected in order to provide the requested goods or services. However, the notification requirement of rule 4.18A would apply."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2e78a5341dfefb990b5c82b4b45c761afed03031e6067d73ab813e9d851e1f43" ;
    values:partOf concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-9 ;
    cof:pageNumber "60"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Collection consent must be withdrawn for request to cease being valid." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
