doc:sch-4-sec-4-9-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "4(4) 3  Request for accredited person to seek to collect CDR data" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) The request ceases to be valid if the collection consent is withdrawn. Note: So long as the use consent is not also withdrawn, the accredited person could continue to use CDR data it had already collected in order to provide the requested goods or services. However, the notification requirement of rule 4.18A would apply." ;
    cof:pageNumber "60"^^xsd:integer .

concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-9-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "4(5) 3  Request for accredited person to seek to collect CDR data"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-4-9-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) If an accredited person asks for a CDR consumer’s consents for the purpose of making a consumer data request under this Part, the accredited person must do so in accordance with Division 4.3. Note: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)." ;
    skos:definition "(5) If an accredited person asks for a CDR consumer’s consents for the purpose of making a consumer data request under this Part, the accredited person must do so in accordance with Division 4.3. Note: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f36ddd0275b0f5fa5b5825d84ce5f76cbd90e6a97a62a5fd3223ab151063af8b" ;
    values:partOf concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-9 ;
    cof:pageNumber "60"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Accredited person must seek CDR consumer's consent in accordance with Division 4.3." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
