doc:sch-4-sec-4-22 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "4 9  Object" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "The object of this Division is to ensure that a consent is: (a) voluntary; and (b) express; and (c) informed; and (d) specific as to purpose; and (e) time limited; and (f) easily withdrawn. Subdivision 4.3.2—Giving consents Note: Under rule 4.3, if an accredited person asks a CDR consumer for their consent to collect and use their CDR data, it must do so in accordance with this Division, and in particular, rules 4.10, 4.11 and 4.12. A failure to do so could contravene one or more civil penalty provisions: see section 56EF of the Act and rule 4.3." ;
    cof:pageNumber "68"^^xsd:integer .

concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-23 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "4 10  Requirements relating to seeking consent"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-4-23 ;
    values:originalText "A request by an accredited person for a CDR consumer to give or amend a consent: (a) must comply with any relevant data standards; and (b) having regard to any consumer experience guidelines made by the Data Standards Body—must be reasonably easy to understand, including by use of plain concise language and, where appropriate, visual aids; and (c) must not include or refer to the accredited person’s CDR policy or other documents in a way that reduces understandability; and (d) must not be combined with other requests except for a consent under these rules (other than a request for direct marketing or de-identification consent)." ;
    skos:definition "A request by an accredited person for a CDR consumer to give or amend a consent: (a) must comply with any relevant data standards; and (b) having regard to any consumer experience guidelines made by the Data Standards Body—must be reasonably easy to understand, including by use of plain concise language and, where appropriate, visual aids; and (c) must not include or refer to the accredited person’s CDR policy or other documents in a way that reduces understandability; and (d) must not be combined with other requests except for a consent under these rules (other than a request for direct marketing or de-identification consent)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "87686f55a4e2325f27eff01284c4b21195342e9c6ffa96e23feedbfa9cbec2c8" ;
    cof:pageNumber "68"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Request for consent must comply with data standards and be easy to understand." ;
    dc:description "Reasonable ease of understanding" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.68" ;
    cml:asserts concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-23-norm .
