concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-29 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "4 13  Withdrawal of consents"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-4-29 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A CDR consumer who has given a consent to an accredited person for the purposes of this Division may withdraw the consent at any time: (a) by using the accredited person’s consumer dashboard; or (b) by using a simple alternative method of communication to be made available by the accredited person for that purpose. (2) If the consent is withdrawn under paragraph (1)(b), the accredited person must give effect to the withdrawal as soon as practicable, and in any case within 2 business days after receiving the communication. Note: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8). (3) Withdrawal of a consent does not affect an election under rule 4.16 that the CDR consumer’s collected CDR data be deleted once it becomes redundant." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A CDR consumer who has given a consent to an accredited person for the purposes of this Division may withdraw the consent at any time: (a) by using the accredited person’s consumer dashboard; or (b) by using a simple alternative method of communication to be made available by the accredited person for that purpose. (2) If the consent is withdrawn under paragraph (1)(b), the accredited person must give effect to the withdrawal as soon as practicable, and in any case within 2 business days after receiving the communication. Note: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8). (3) Withdrawal of a consent does not affect an election under rule 4.16 that the CDR consumer’s collected CDR data be deleted once it becomes redundant."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "91985f8cc1597f95a05604cbf31d4ad0699805833cb59712390fb4e1363f2ec6" ;
    cof:pageNumber "73"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-29-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-29-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-29-ss-3 ;
