concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-31-ss-3 cml:asserts concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-31-ss-3-logic-deontic-1 .
concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-31-ss-3-logic-deontic-1 a cml:LogicApplication ;
    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    cml:operator "Prohibition" ;
    cml:logicSummary "Prohibits collection consent expiration upon notification." ;
    cml:premiseText "(3) If: (a) an accredited person is notified by a data holder, under rule 4.26A, of the withdrawal of an authorisation to disclose CDR data that relates to a collection consent given under this Division; and (b) the collection consent has not expired in accordance with subrule (1); the collection consent expires when the accredited person receives that notification." ;
    cml:conclusionText "(3) If: (a) an accredited person is notified by a data holder, under rule 4.26A, of the defaulted consent; and (b) the consent has not expired in accordance with subrule (1); the consent expires when the accredited person receives that notification." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sch-4-sec-4-31-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "4(3) 13(1)(a)―when the consent was withdrawn;" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) If: (a) an accredited person is notified by a data holder, under rule 4.26A, of the withdrawal of an authorisation to disclose CDR data that relates to a collection consent given under this Division; and (b) the collection consent has not expired in accordance with subrule (1); the collection consent expires when the accredited person receives that notification. Note: This would not result in the use consent relating to any CDR data that had already been collected expiring. However, see the notification requirement of rule 4.18A." ;
    cof:pageNumber "74"^^xsd:integer .

concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-31-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "4(4) 13(1)(a)―when the consent was withdrawn;"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-4-31-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) If: (a) an accredited person has a collection consent given under this Division to collect particular CDR data from a particular accredited data recipient; and (b) the accredited data recipient has an AP disclosure consent to disclose that CDR data to that accredited person; then if one of those consents expires, the other expires when the accredited person or accredited data recipient is notified of the first-mentioned expiry. Note: The notification is required by rule 4.18B.   Consumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4 Giving and amending consents—accredited persons  Division 4.3 Section 4.15 Competition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020" ;
    skos:definition "(4) If: (a) an accredited person has a collection consent given under this Division to collect particular CDR data from a particular accredited data recipient; and (b) the accredited data recipient has an AP disclosure consent to disclose that CDR data to that accredited person; then if one of those consents expires, the other expires when the accredited person or accredited data recipient is notified of the first-mentioned expiry. Note: The notification is required by rule 4.18B.   Consumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4 Giving and amending consents—accredited persons  Division 4.3 Section 4.15 Competition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "22af4b92b385948be6b4c41f27ee0d4ad25c9b3e6de339fac032e94f91157e12" ;
    values:partOf concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-31 ;
