concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-39 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "4 18B  Notification if collection consent or AP disclosure consent expires"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-4-39 ;
    values:originalText "(1) This rule applies if: (a) an accredited person has made a consumer data request to an accredited data recipient on behalf of a CDR representative, based on a collection consent given under this Division relating to particular CDR data and that accredited data recipient; and (b) the accredited data recipient has an AP disclosure consent relating to that CDR data; and (c) the request has not been completely resolved. (2) If the collection consent expires in accordance with these rules, the accredited person must notify the accredited data recipient as soon as practicable of the expiry. Note 1: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8). Note 2: The AP disclosure consent that the accredited data recipient has expires when the notification is received—see subrule 4.14(4)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This rule applies if: (a) an accredited person has made a consumer data request to an accredited data recipient on behalf of a CDR representative, based on a collection consent given under this Division relating to particular CDR data and that accredited data recipient; and (b) the accredited data recipient has an AP disclosure consent relating to that CDR data; and (c) the request has not been completely resolved. (2) If the collection consent expires in accordance with these rules, the accredited person must notify the accredited data recipient as soon as practicable of the expiry. Note 1: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8). Note 2: The AP disclosure consent that the accredited data recipient has expires when the notification is received—see subrule 4.14(4)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b6a7b1e89d716dca089398a6ff6b2737df274b8dc4402e1c7d7d8a1db370bda6" ;
    cof:pageNumber "77"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-39-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-39-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.77" .
doc:sch-4-sec-4-39 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "4 18B  Notification if collection consent or AP disclosure consent expires" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) This rule applies if: (a) an accredited person has made a consumer data request to an accredited data recipient on behalf of a CDR representative, based on a collection consent given under this Division relating to particular CDR data and that accredited data recipient; and (b) the accredited data recipient has an AP disclosure consent relating to that CDR data; and (c) the request has not been completely resolved. (2) If the collection consent expires in accordance with these rules, the accredited person must notify the accredited data recipient as soon as practicable of the expiry. Note 1: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8). Note 2: The AP disclosure consent that the accredited data recipient has expires when the notification is received—see subrule 4.14(4)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "77"^^xsd:integer .

