concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-40 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "4 18C  Notification of data holder or accredited data recipient if collection"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-4-40 ;
    values:originalText "consent is amended (1) This rule applies if: (a) an accredited person has made a consumer data request to a CDR participant, based on a collection consent given under this Division relating to particular CDR data and that CDR participant; and (b) the request has not been completely resolved; and (c) the CDR consumer amends the consent. (2) The accredited person must notify: (a) if the CDR participant is a data holder―the data holder, in accordance with the data standards, that the consent has been amended; and (b) if the CDR participant is an accredited data recipient―the accredited data recipient as soon as practicable that the consent has been amended. Note: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)." ;
    skos:definition "consent is amended (1) This rule applies if: (a) an accredited person has made a consumer data request to a CDR participant, based on a collection consent given under this Division relating to particular CDR data and that CDR participant; and (b) the request has not been completely resolved; and (c) the CDR consumer amends the consent. (2) The accredited person must notify: (a) if the CDR participant is a data holder―the data holder, in accordance with the data standards, that the consent has been amended; and (b) if the CDR participant is an accredited data recipient―the accredited data recipient as soon as practicable that the consent has been amended. Note: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d3b619248696160abe6fd7862f5c41b14b9558991360fbd22e713a2d3d924762" ;
    cof:pageNumber "78"^^xsd:integer ;
