concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-42 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "4 20  Ongoing notification requirement—current consents"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-4-42 ;
    values:originalText "(1) This rule applies in relation to a collection consent, use consent or disclosure consent given under this Division if: (a) the consent is current; and (b) 90 days have elapsed since the latest of the following: (i) the CDR consumer gave the consent; (ia) the CDR consumer last amended the consent; (ii) the CDR consumer last used their consumer dashboard; (iii) the accredited person last notified the CDR consumer that the consent is still current. (2) The accredited person must notify the CDR consumer, in relation to each consent given by the CDR consumer that is still current, that the consent is still current.   Consumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4 Giving and amending consents—accredited persons  Division 4.3 Section 4.20A Competition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020 Note: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8). (3) The notification must be given in accordance with the data standards. Note: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This rule applies in relation to a collection consent, use consent or disclosure consent given under this Division if: (a) the consent is current; and (b) 90 days have elapsed since the latest of the following: (i) the CDR consumer gave the consent; (ia) the CDR consumer last amended the consent; (ii) the CDR consumer last used their consumer dashboard; (iii) the accredited person last notified the CDR consumer that the consent is still current. (2) The accredited person must notify the CDR consumer, in relation to each consent given by the CDR consumer that is still current, that the consent is still current.   Consumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4 Giving and amending consents—accredited persons  Division 4.3 Section 4.20A Competition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020 Note: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8). (3) The notification must be given in accordance with the data standards. Note: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f2238d420ceac42bb912f0e329421df61f57ff687c28291a14364b7c749ad3b2" ;
    cof:pageNumber "78"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-42-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-42-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-42-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
