doc:sch-4-sec-4-52-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "4(3) 20H  Inviting CDR consumer to amend consent" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) The CDR representative may invite a CDR consumer to amend a current consent if: (a) the amendment would better enable the CDR representative to provide the goods or services referred to in paragraph 4.3A(1)(a); or (b) the amendment would: (i) be consequential to an agreement between the CDR representative and the CDR consumer to modify those goods or services; and (ii) enable the CDR representative to provide the modified goods or services." ;
    cof:pageNumber "84"^^xsd:integer .

concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-52-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "4(4) 20H  Inviting CDR consumer to amend consent"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-4-52-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) The CDR representative must not, for an invitation to amend the period referred to in paragraph 4.20E(1)(b): (a) give the invitation any earlier than a reasonable period before the current consent is expected to expire; or (b) give more than a reasonable number of such invitations within this period." ;
    skos:definition "(4) The CDR representative must not, for an invitation to amend the period referred to in paragraph 4.20E(1)(b): (a) give the invitation any earlier than a reasonable period before the current consent is expected to expire; or (b) give more than a reasonable number of such invitations within this period."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "542d629ac3859f728964c76b759df838824903c74373543aa477f872338c1708" ;
