    values:originalText "(3) If: (a) a CDR representative principal has a collection consent given under this Division to collect particular CDR data from a particular accredited data recipient; and (b) the accredited data recipient has an AP disclosure consent to disclose that CDR data to that CDR representative principal; then if one of those consents expires, the other expires when the CDR representative principal or accredited data recipient is notified of the first-mentioned expiry. Note: The notification is required by rule 4.18B.   Consumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4 Giving and amending consents—CDR representatives  Division 4.3A Section 4.20L Competition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020" ;
