    values:originalText "For paragraph 4.20E(3)(i), the additional information relating to de-identification is the following: (a) what the CDR data de-identification process is; (b) if it would disclose (by sale or otherwise) the de-identified data to one or more other persons; (i) that fact; and (ii) the classes of persons to which it would disclose that data; and (iii) why it would so disclose that data; (c) if the CDR representative would use the de-identified data for general research―that fact, together with a link to a description in the CDR representative principal’s CDR policy of: (i) the research to be conducted; and (ii) any additional benefit to be provided to the CDR consumer for consenting to the use; (e) that the CDR consumer would not be able to elect, in accordance with rule" ;
