concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-65 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "4 20P  Notification of data holder or accredited data recipient if collection"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-4-65 ;
    values:originalText "consent expires (1) This rule applies if:   Consumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4 Giving and amending consents—CDR representatives  Division 4.3A Section 4.20Q Competition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020 (a) an accredited person has made a consumer data request on behalf of a CDR representative to a CDR participant based on a collection consent given under this Division relating to particular CDR data and a particular CDR participant; and (b) the request has not been completely resolved; and (c) the consent expires for any reason. (2) The accredited person must notify: (a) if the CDR participant is a data holder―the data holder, in accordance with the data standards, that the consent has expired; and (b) if the CDR participant is an accredited data recipient―the accredited data recipient as soon as practicable that the consent has expired. Note: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)." ;
    skos:definition "consent expires (1) This rule applies if:   Consumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4 Giving and amending consents—CDR representatives  Division 4.3A Section 4.20Q Competition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020 (a) an accredited person has made a consumer data request on behalf of a CDR representative to a CDR participant based on a collection consent given under this Division relating to particular CDR data and a particular CDR participant; and (b) the request has not been completely resolved; and (c) the consent expires for any reason. (2) The accredited person must notify: (a) if the CDR participant is a data holder―the data holder, in accordance with the data standards, that the consent has expired; and (b) if the CDR participant is an accredited data recipient―the accredited data recipient as soon as practicable that the consent has expired. Note: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8521cb8484fae9a3d841236f2847a443e9d051b12cb779c0960222e34db90eca" ;
    cof:pageNumber "88"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-65-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-65-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
