doc:sch-4-sec-4-68-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "4(1) 20S  Notification if collection consent is amended" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) This rule applies if: (a) a CDR representative principal has made a consumer data request to a CDR participant on behalf of a CDR representative, based on a collection consent given under this Division relating to particular CDR data and a particular CDR participant; and (b) the request has not been completely resolved; and (c) the CDR consumer amends the consent." ;
    cof:pageNumber "90"^^xsd:integer .

concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-68-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "4(2) 20S  Notification if collection consent is amended"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-4-68-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The CDR representative principal must notify: (a) if the CDR participant is a data holder―the data holder, in accordance with the data standards, that the consent has been amended; and (b) if the CDR participant is an accredited data recipient―the accredited data recipient as soon as practicable that the consent has been amended. Note: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)." ;
    skos:definition "(2) The CDR representative principal must notify: (a) if the CDR participant is a data holder―the data holder, in accordance with the data standards, that the consent has been amended; and (b) if the CDR participant is an accredited data recipient―the accredited data recipient as soon as practicable that the consent has been amended. Note: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c046f06d63791d7f5fe97fcca696f550405573af438ee39f8753023d8041a368" ;
    values:partOf concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-68 ;
    cof:pageNumber "90"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Notify data holder and accredited data recipient of amended consent" ;
    dc:description "Notification" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
