    skos:definition "(1) This rule applies in relation to a collection consent, use consent or disclosure consent given under this Division if:   Consumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4 Giving and amending consents—CDR representatives  Division 4.3A Section 4.20U Competition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020 (a) the consent is current; and (b) 90 days have elapsed since the latest of the following: (i) the CDR consumer gave the consent; (ii) the CDR consumer last amended the consent; (iii) the CDR consumer last used the CDR representative principal’s consumer dashboard; (iv) the CDR representative or the CDR representative principal last notified the CDR consumer that the consent is still current."@en ;
