    cml:operator "MUST" ;
    cml:logicSummary "CDR representative or principal must notify CDR consumer" ;
    cml:premiseText "The consent is current and at least 90 days old." ;
    cml:conclusionText "The CDR representative or principal must notify the CDR consumer." ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sch-4-sec-4-71-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "4(1) 20U  Ongoing notification requirement—current consents" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) This rule applies in relation to a collection consent, use consent or disclosure consent given under this Division if:   Consumer data requests made by accredited persons  Part 4 Giving and amending consents—CDR representatives  Division 4.3A Section 4.20U Competition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020 (a) the consent is current; and (b) 90 days have elapsed since the latest of the following: (i) the CDR consumer gave the consent; (ii) the CDR consumer last amended the consent; (iii) the CDR consumer last used the CDR representative principal’s consumer dashboard; (iv) the CDR representative or the CDR representative principal last notified the CDR consumer that the consent is still current." ;
    cof:pageNumber "90"^^xsd:integer .

concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-71-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "4(2) 20U  Ongoing notification requirement—current consents"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-4-71-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The CDR representative must notify the CDR consumer, in relation to each consent given by the CDR consumer that is still current, that the consent is still current. Note: A failure to do this could make the CDR representative principal liable for a civil penalty (see rule 1.16A)." ;
    skos:definition "(2) The CDR representative must notify the CDR consumer, in relation to each consent given by the CDR consumer that is still current, that the consent is still current. Note: A failure to do this could make the CDR representative principal liable for a civil penalty (see rule 1.16A)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "49302d801c4880799b0d50b16ec9aa2bc45f447110ee8c85a7fd41fe142b5a66" ;
    values:partOf concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-71 ;
