concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-25 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "5 19  Suspension of accreditation—duration"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-5-25 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Without limitation, the CDR Accreditor, under rule 5.17: (a) may suspend an accreditation: (i) for a period of time that ends at a specified date; or (ii) for a period of time that ends with the occurrence of a specified event; and (b) may, subject to the same conditions on which an accreditation was suspended, extend the suspension. (2) The CDR Accreditor may, in writing, at any time, remove a suspension." ;
    skos:definition "(1) Without limitation, the CDR Accreditor, under rule 5.17: (a) may suspend an accreditation: (i) for a period of time that ends at a specified date; or (ii) for a period of time that ends with the occurrence of a specified event; and (b) may, subject to the same conditions on which an accreditation was suspended, extend the suspension. (2) The CDR Accreditor may, in writing, at any time, remove a suspension."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a97b1a7cd65474c96cc5cec553a7a314b2dac0b6f2d51bdff171d93642a25086" ;
    cof:pageNumber "115"^^xsd:integer ;
