doc:sch-4-sec-5-26-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "5(2) 20  General process for suspension of accreditation or extension of suspension" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) Before suspending an accreditation under rule 5.17, or extending a suspension, the CDR Accreditor must: (a) inform the accredited person of: (i) the proposed suspension or extension (including the proposed duration); and (ii) in the case of a suspension—when it is proposed to take effect; and (b) give the accredited person a reasonable opportunity to be heard in relation to the proposed suspension or extension." ;
    cof:pageNumber "115"^^xsd:integer .

concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-26-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "5(3) 20  General process for suspension of accreditation or extension of suspension"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-5-26-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) If the Accreditor suspends an accredited person’s accreditation under rule 5.17, the Accreditor must notify the person, in writing, of the suspension and the period of the suspension. Note: The decision to suspend an accredited person’s accreditation can be reviewed by the Administrative Appeals Tribunal: see paragraph 9.2(b)." ;
    skos:definition "(3) If the Accreditor suspends an accredited person’s accreditation under rule 5.17, the Accreditor must notify the person, in writing, of the suspension and the period of the suspension. Note: The decision to suspend an accredited person’s accreditation can be reviewed by the Administrative Appeals Tribunal: see paragraph 9.2(b)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "fcace94fa068bd3b73347856ca48da7ac0ec774e70291ce1e07834f748c3ddad" ;
    values:partOf concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-26 ;
    cof:pageNumber "115"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Accreditor must notify accredited person of suspension and period." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
