    cof:title "5(4) 23  Consequences of surrender, suspension or revocation of accreditation" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) If: (a) the person’s accreditation has been surrendered or revoked; and (b) the person has collected CDR data under these rules; and (c) the person is not required to retain that CDR data by or under an Australian law or a court/tribunal order; and (d) the CDR data does not relate to any current or anticipated: (i) legal proceedings; or (ii) dispute resolution proceedings; to which the person is a party; and (e) where there is a CDR consumer for the CDR data, the CDR data does not relate to any current or anticipated: (i) legal proceedings; or (ii) dispute resolution proceedings; to which the CDR consumer is a party; the person must delete or de-identify that data by taking the steps specified in rule 7.12 or 7.13, as appropriate. Note 1: In addition: • if an accreditation is revoked or surrendered: - any consents to collect and use CDR data expire: see subrules 4.14(6) and" ;
    cof:pageNumber "116"^^xsd:integer .

concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-4-86 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "4 20K(2); and"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-4-86 ;
    values:originalText "- any authorisations to disclose CDR data expire: see subrule 4.26(2); and • if an accreditation is suspended, the accredited person is not able to collect data while the suspension is in effect. Note 2: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8). (5) For the purposes of paragraph (4)(e), if paragraphs (4)(a) to (d) apply in relation to the CDR data of the CDR consumer, the person may: (a) request the CDR consumer to state whether or not such proceedings are current or anticipated; and (b) rely on that statement." ;
    skos:definition "- any authorisations to disclose CDR data expire: see subrule 4.26(2); and • if an accreditation is suspended, the accredited person is not able to collect data while the suspension is in effect. Note 2: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8). (5) For the purposes of paragraph (4)(e), if paragraphs (4)(a) to (d) apply in relation to the CDR data of the CDR consumer, the person may: (a) request the CDR consumer to state whether or not such proceedings are current or anticipated; and (b) rely on that statement."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "83d137d8bcc6700efb3c2d9fd8db6e0701a951f99c4e553db00c667f780ddd93" ;
    cof:pageNumber "117"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Disclosing CDR data without authorization is prohibited." ;
