concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-36 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "5 30  Other functions of Accreditation Registrar"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-5-36 ;
    values:originalText "For paragraph 56CL(1)(b) of the Act, the other functions of the Accreditation Registrar include the following:   Rules relating to accreditation etc.  Part 5 Rules relating to Register of Accredited Persons  Division 5.3 Section 5.31 Competition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020 (a) enabling information included in the Register of Accredited Persons and associated database to be communicated to data holders and accredited persons to facilitate the making and processing of requests under these rules in accordance with these rules and the data standards; (b) maintaining the security, integrity and stability of the Register and associated database, including undertaking or facilitating any testing by CDR participants for that purpose; (c) requesting a data holder or an accredited person to do specified things where that is necessary or convenient in order for the Accreditation Registrar to perform its functions or exercise its powers; Example: The Accreditation Registrar could request data holders or accredited persons to undertake and complete testing where it is necessary or convenient for the Registrar to perform its functions under paragraph (b). (d) informing the CDR Accreditor of any failure of an accredited person to comply with a condition of its accreditation or to do things requested by the Registrar in the performance of its functions or the exercise of its powers. Note: The Accreditation Registrar has the power to do all things necessary or convenient to be done for or in connection with the performance of its functions. See subsection 56CL(2) of the Act." ;
    skos:definition "For paragraph 56CL(1)(b) of the Act, the other functions of the Accreditation Registrar include the following:   Rules relating to accreditation etc.  Part 5 Rules relating to Register of Accredited Persons  Division 5.3 Section 5.31 Competition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020 (a) enabling information included in the Register of Accredited Persons and associated database to be communicated to data holders and accredited persons to facilitate the making and processing of requests under these rules in accordance with these rules and the data standards; (b) maintaining the security, integrity and stability of the Register and associated database, including undertaking or facilitating any testing by CDR participants for that purpose; (c) requesting a data holder or an accredited person to do specified things where that is necessary or convenient in order for the Accreditation Registrar to perform its functions or exercise its powers; Example: The Accreditation Registrar could request data holders or accredited persons to undertake and complete testing where it is necessary or convenient for the Registrar to perform its functions under paragraph (b). (d) informing the CDR Accreditor of any failure of an accredited person to comply with a condition of its accreditation or to do things requested by the Registrar in the performance of its functions or the exercise of its powers. Note: The Accreditation Registrar has the power to do all things necessary or convenient to be done for or in connection with the performance of its functions. See subsection 56CL(2) of the Act."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b632fcbeba453245e5e31210249ff52183ae3d0df7f8227cd070892857d4d240" ;
    cof:pageNumber "120"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The Accreditation Registrar must inform the CDR Accreditor of any failure of an accredited person to comply with a condition of its accreditation." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.120" ;
    cml:asserts concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-5-36-norm .
