concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-6 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "7 3B  Rule relating to privacy safeguard 4—destruction of unsolicited data—"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-7-6 ;
    values:originalText "outsourced service providers (1) An accredited person breaches this subrule if a direct or indirect OSP of: (a) the accredited person; or (b) a CDR representative of the accredited person; fails to comply with section 56EG of the Act in relation to service data of a CDR consumer as if: (c) it were an accredited person; and (d) it had collected the service data. Note 1: See rule 1.10 for the definition of “service data” in relation to a CDR outsourcing arrangement. Note 2: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8). (2) For subrule (1), it is irrelevant whether the action of the direct or indirect OSP in relation to the service data is in accordance with the CDR outsourcing arrangement.   Rules relating to privacy safeguards  Part 7 Rules relating to privacy safeguards  Division 7.2 Section 7.4 Competition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020 Subdivision 7.2.2—Rules relating to collecting CDR data" ;
    skos:definition "outsourced service providers (1) An accredited person breaches this subrule if a direct or indirect OSP of: (a) the accredited person; or (b) a CDR representative of the accredited person; fails to comply with section 56EG of the Act in relation to service data of a CDR consumer as if: (c) it were an accredited person; and (d) it had collected the service data. Note 1: See rule 1.10 for the definition of “service data” in relation to a CDR outsourcing arrangement. Note 2: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8). (2) For subrule (1), it is irrelevant whether the action of the direct or indirect OSP in relation to the service data is in accordance with the CDR outsourcing arrangement.   Rules relating to privacy safeguards  Part 7 Rules relating to privacy safeguards  Division 7.2 Section 7.4 Competition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020 Subdivision 7.2.2—Rules relating to collecting CDR data"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d402bce21b9aa67e5abb94c66fd4c8f2244778bc6a2e786afbecc5da9f09473c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "128"^^xsd:integer ;
