    values:originalText "(1) An accredited person breaches this subrule if a direct or indirect OSP of: (a) the accredited person; or (b) a CDR representative of the accredited person; fails to comply with section 56EG of the Act in relation to service data of a CDR consumer as if: (c) it were an accredited person; and (d) it had collected the service data. Note 1: See rule 1.10 for the definition of “service data” in relation to a CDR outsourcing arrangement. Note 2: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) An accredited person breaches this subrule if a direct or indirect OSP of: (a) the accredited person; or (b) a CDR representative of the accredited person; fails to comply with section 56EG of the Act in relation to service data of a CDR consumer as if: (c) it were an accredited person; and (d) it had collected the service data. Note 1: See rule 1.10 for the definition of “service data” in relation to a CDR outsourcing arrangement. Note 2: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "33395801a848cf3a5e71f1e7132a7398d8931e0b57b11519f140d1038ebfdbbf" ;
