concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-7 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "7 Section 7"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-7-7 ;
    values:originalText "4  Rule relating to privacy safeguard 5—notifying of the collection of CDR data (1) For section 56EH of the Act, and subject to subrule (2), an accredited data recipient that collected the CDR data in accordance with section 56EF of the Act as a result of a collection consent must update the person’s consumer dashboard as soon as practicable to indicate: (a) what CDR data was collected; and (b) when the CDR data was collected; and (c) the CDR participant for the CDR data from which the CDR data was collected. (2) Where the CDR data was collected by a sponsor on behalf of an affiliate: (a) the sponsor is not required to provide the consumer dashboard; and Note: The affiliate, as an accredited person that makes the consumer request through the sponsor, is required to provide the consumer dashboard under subrule 1.14(1). (b) the sponsor and the affiliate may choose which of them will be responsible for updating the consumer’s dashboard in accordance with subrule (1); and (c) the dashboard must also indicate that the CDR data was collected by the sponsor on behalf of the affiliate. Note 1: See also paragraph 1.14(3)(ha). Note 2: See subrule 1.16(5) for how this rule applies where the CDR data is collected by an accredited person acting as a direct or indirect OSP to the accredited data recipient. Subdivision 7.2.3—Rules relating to dealing with CDR data" ;
    skos:definition "4  Rule relating to privacy safeguard 5—notifying of the collection of CDR data (1) For section 56EH of the Act, and subject to subrule (2), an accredited data recipient that collected the CDR data in accordance with section 56EF of the Act as a result of a collection consent must update the person’s consumer dashboard as soon as practicable to indicate: (a) what CDR data was collected; and (b) when the CDR data was collected; and (c) the CDR participant for the CDR data from which the CDR data was collected. (2) Where the CDR data was collected by a sponsor on behalf of an affiliate: (a) the sponsor is not required to provide the consumer dashboard; and Note: The affiliate, as an accredited person that makes the consumer request through the sponsor, is required to provide the consumer dashboard under subrule 1.14(1). (b) the sponsor and the affiliate may choose which of them will be responsible for updating the consumer’s dashboard in accordance with subrule (1); and (c) the dashboard must also indicate that the CDR data was collected by the sponsor on behalf of the affiliate. Note 1: See also paragraph 1.14(3)(ha). Note 2: See subrule 1.16(5) for how this rule applies where the CDR data is collected by an accredited person acting as a direct or indirect OSP to the accredited data recipient. Subdivision 7.2.3—Rules relating to dealing with CDR data"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "901f82e10abd827be82644f129a9b4eb48066f535e101a7131493022d193766e" ;
    cof:pageNumber "129"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-7-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-7-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.129" .
doc:sch-4-sec-7-7 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "7 Section 7" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "4  Rule relating to privacy safeguard 5—notifying of the collection of CDR data (1) For section 56EH of the Act, and subject to subrule (2), an accredited data recipient that collected the CDR data in accordance with section 56EF of the Act as a result of a collection consent must update the person’s consumer dashboard as soon as practicable to indicate: (a) what CDR data was collected; and (b) when the CDR data was collected; and (c) the CDR participant for the CDR data from which the CDR data was collected. (2) Where the CDR data was collected by a sponsor on behalf of an affiliate: (a) the sponsor is not required to provide the consumer dashboard; and Note: The affiliate, as an accredited person that makes the consumer request through the sponsor, is required to provide the consumer dashboard under subrule 1.14(1). (b) the sponsor and the affiliate may choose which of them will be responsible for updating the consumer’s dashboard in accordance with subrule (1); and (c) the dashboard must also indicate that the CDR data was collected by the sponsor on behalf of the affiliate. Note 1: See also paragraph 1.14(3)(ha). Note 2: See subrule 1.16(5) for how this rule applies where the CDR data is collected by an accredited person acting as a direct or indirect OSP to the accredited data recipient. Subdivision 7.2.3—Rules relating to dealing with CDR data" ;
    cof:pageNumber "129"^^xsd:integer .

concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-7-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "7(1) Section 7"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-7-7-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) For section 56EH of the Act, and subject to subrule (2), an accredited data recipient that collected the CDR data in accordance with section 56EF of the Act as a result of a collection consent must update the person’s consumer dashboard as soon as practicable to indicate: (a) what CDR data was collected; and (b) when the CDR data was collected; and (c) the CDR participant for the CDR data from which the CDR data was collected." ;
    skos:definition "(1) For section 56EH of the Act, and subject to subrule (2), an accredited data recipient that collected the CDR data in accordance with section 56EF of the Act as a result of a collection consent must update the person’s consumer dashboard as soon as practicable to indicate: (a) what CDR data was collected; and (b) when the CDR data was collected; and (c) the CDR participant for the CDR data from which the CDR data was collected."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "69c24c5db7b5e353cab26281b99c9c8ef47abfcb30c22dbba22e5b0c8584f6ea" ;
