    skos:definition "(2) An accredited person breaches this subrule if a direct or indirect OSP of: (a) the accredited person; or (b) a CDR representative of the accredited person; fails to comply with section 56EL of the Act in relation to service data of a CDR consumer as if it were an accredited data recipient of the service data. Note 1: See rule 1.10AA for the definition of “service data” in relation to a CDR representative arrangement. Note 2: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)."@en ;
