doc:sch-4-sec-7-14-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "7(2) Section 7" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) An accredited person breaches this subrule if a direct or indirect OSP of: (a) the accredited person; or (b) a CDR representative of the accredited person; fails to comply with section 56EL of the Act in relation to service data of a CDR consumer as if it were an accredited data recipient of the service data. Note 1: See rule 1.10AA for the definition of “service data” in relation to a CDR representative arrangement. Note 2: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "134"^^xsd:integer .

concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-15 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "7 9  Rule relating to privacy safeguard 10—notifying of the disclosure of CDR"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-7-15 ;
    values:originalText "data (1) For subsection 56EM(1) of the Act, a data holder that discloses CDR data to an accredited person as a result of a consumer data request must, as soon as practicable, update each consumer dashboard that relates to the request to indicate: (a) what CDR data was disclosed; and (b) when the CDR data was disclosed; and (c) the accredited data recipient, identified in accordance with any entry on the Register of Accredited Persons specified as being for that purpose. Note 1: For correction requests, see section 56EP of the Act (privacy safeguard 13) and Subdivision 7.2.5 of these rules.   Rules relating to privacy safeguards  Part 7 Rules relating to privacy safeguards  Division 7.2 Section 7.10 Competition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020 Note 2: If a consumer data request is made that relates to a joint account, the other joint account holder’s consumer dashboard may not be required to be similarly updated. See rule" ;
    skos:definition "data (1) For subsection 56EM(1) of the Act, a data holder that discloses CDR data to an accredited person as a result of a consumer data request must, as soon as practicable, update each consumer dashboard that relates to the request to indicate: (a) what CDR data was disclosed; and (b) when the CDR data was disclosed; and (c) the accredited data recipient, identified in accordance with any entry on the Register of Accredited Persons specified as being for that purpose. Note 1: For correction requests, see section 56EP of the Act (privacy safeguard 13) and Subdivision 7.2.5 of these rules.   Rules relating to privacy safeguards  Part 7 Rules relating to privacy safeguards  Division 7.2 Section 7.10 Competition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020 Note 2: If a consumer data request is made that relates to a joint account, the other joint account holder’s consumer dashboard may not be required to be similarly updated. See rule"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "19b298d6e36d8c357f050416bc5c02fe0da46f3954276674e9e6ac80459b6803" ;
    cof:pageNumber "134"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Update consumer dashboard with disclosed CDR data and recipient information." ;
    dc:description "yes" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.134" ;
    cml:asserts concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-7-15-norm .
