doc:sch-4-sec-8-10 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "8 3  Functions of Data Standards Advisory Committee" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "The function of a Data Standards Advisory Committee is to advise the Data Standards Chair about: (a) any matters identified in the instrument establishing the Committee; and (b) any other matter referred to the Committee by the Chair." ;
    cof:pageNumber "141"^^xsd:integer .

concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-8-11 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "8 4  Appointment to Data Standards Advisory Committee"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-8-11 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Data Standards Chair: (a) must appoint to a Data Standards Advisory Committee: (i) 1 or more consumer representatives; and (ii) 1 or more privacy representatives; and (b) may appoint others to the Committee as the Chair sees fit. (2) An appointment must be in writing. (3) Remuneration is not payable in respect of an appointment to a Data Standards Advisory Committee. The Chair may determine any other terms and conditions of an appointment in writing. Note: An appointee may be reappointed: see section 33AA of the Act Interpretation Act 1901 and paragraph 13(1)(a) of the Legislation Act 2003." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Data Standards Chair: (a) must appoint to a Data Standards Advisory Committee: (i) 1 or more consumer representatives; and (ii) 1 or more privacy representatives; and (b) may appoint others to the Committee as the Chair sees fit. (2) An appointment must be in writing. (3) Remuneration is not payable in respect of an appointment to a Data Standards Advisory Committee. The Chair may determine any other terms and conditions of an appointment in writing. Note: An appointee may be reappointed: see section 33AA of the Act Interpretation Act 1901 and paragraph 13(1)(a) of the Legislation Act 2003."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "66c9ab19e81f2c30f00cb7fe23280d2400d54bcd4e9dbec1470c8346bb538157" ;
