concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-8 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "9 3  Records to be kept and maintained"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-9-8 ;
    values:originalText "Records to be kept and maintained—data holder (1) A data holder must keep and maintain records that record and explain the following: (a) authorisations given by CDR consumers to disclose CDR data; (b) amendments to or withdrawals of authorisations to disclose CDR data; (c) notifications of withdrawals of consents to collect CDR data; (ca) where the data holder is a primary data holder—any requests for SR data made under subrule 1.23(4) and responses received under subrule 1.23(5) or (6); (cb) where the data holder is a secondary data holder: (i) any requests for SR data received under subrule 1.22(3) or 1.23(4) and responses given under subrule 1.22(4) or (5) or 1.23(5) or (6); and (ii) where the data holder has refused to disclose requested SR data—the reasons relied upon to refuse to disclose the SR data, including any rule or data standard; (d) disclosures of CDR data made in response to consumer data requests; (da) any written agreement of a kind referred to in subrule 2.4(5) the data holder has entered into; (db) any election by the data holder in effect under subclause 7.1A(1) of Schedule 3; (e) instances where the data holder has refused to disclose requested CDR data and the rule or data standard relied upon to refuse to disclose the CDR data; (f) CDR complaint data; (fa) CDR consumer complaints; (g) the processes by which the data holder asks CDR consumers for their authorisation to disclose CDR data and for an amendment to their authorisation, including a video of each process. Civil penalty: (a) for an individual―$50,000; and (b) for a body corporate―$250,000. Records to be kept and maintained—accredited data recipient (2) An accredited data recipient must keep and maintain records that record and explain the following: (a) all consents, including, if applicable, the uses of the CDR data that the CDR consumer has consented to under any use consents; (b) amendments to or withdrawals of consents by CDR consumers; (c) notifications of withdrawals of authorisations received from data holders; (d) CDR complaint data;" ;
    skos:definition "Records to be kept and maintained—data holder (1) A data holder must keep and maintain records that record and explain the following: (a) authorisations given by CDR consumers to disclose CDR data; (b) amendments to or withdrawals of authorisations to disclose CDR data; (c) notifications of withdrawals of consents to collect CDR data; (ca) where the data holder is a primary data holder—any requests for SR data made under subrule 1.23(4) and responses received under subrule 1.23(5) or (6); (cb) where the data holder is a secondary data holder: (i) any requests for SR data received under subrule 1.22(3) or 1.23(4) and responses given under subrule 1.22(4) or (5) or 1.23(5) or (6); and (ii) where the data holder has refused to disclose requested SR data—the reasons relied upon to refuse to disclose the SR data, including any rule or data standard; (d) disclosures of CDR data made in response to consumer data requests; (da) any written agreement of a kind referred to in subrule 2.4(5) the data holder has entered into; (db) any election by the data holder in effect under subclause 7.1A(1) of Schedule 3; (e) instances where the data holder has refused to disclose requested CDR data and the rule or data standard relied upon to refuse to disclose the CDR data; (f) CDR complaint data; (fa) CDR consumer complaints; (g) the processes by which the data holder asks CDR consumers for their authorisation to disclose CDR data and for an amendment to their authorisation, including a video of each process. Civil penalty: (a) for an individual―$50,000; and (b) for a body corporate―$250,000. Records to be kept and maintained—accredited data recipient (2) An accredited data recipient must keep and maintain records that record and explain the following: (a) all consents, including, if applicable, the uses of the CDR data that the CDR consumer has consented to under any use consents; (b) amendments to or withdrawals of consents by CDR consumers; (c) notifications of withdrawals of authori"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "daed8a751aa92cd7b9016021ed115d439f06adf445e11459e15ddda814a71b4b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "149"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-8-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-8-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.149" .
doc:sch-4-sec-9-8 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "9 3  Records to be kept and maintained" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Records to be kept and maintained—data holder (1) A data holder must keep and maintain records that record and explain the following: (a) authorisations given by CDR consumers to disclose CDR data; (b) amendments to or withdrawals of authorisations to disclose CDR data; (c) notifications of withdrawals of consents to collect CDR data; (ca) where the data holder is a primary data holder—any requests for SR data made under subrule 1.23(4) and responses received under subrule 1.23(5) or (6); (cb) where the data holder is a secondary data holder: (i) any requests for SR data received under subrule 1.22(3) or 1.23(4) and responses given under subrule 1.22(4) or (5) or 1.23(5) or (6); and (ii) where the data holder has refused to disclose requested SR data—the reasons relied upon to refuse to disclose the SR data, including any rule or data standard; (d) disclosures of CDR data made in response to consumer data requests; (da) any written agreement of a kind referred to in subrule 2.4(5) the data holder has entered into; (db) any election by the data holder in effect under subclause 7.1A(1) of Schedule 3; (e) instances where the data holder has refused to disclose requested CDR data and the rule or data standard relied upon to refuse to disclose the CDR data; (f) CDR complaint data; (fa) CDR consumer complaints; (g) the processes by which the data holder asks CDR consumers for their authorisation to disclose CDR data and for an amendment to their authorisation, including a video of each process. Civil penalty: (a) for an individual―$50,000; and (b) for a body corporate―$250,000. Records to be kept and maintained—accredited data recipient (2) An accredited data recipient must keep and maintain records that record and explain the following: (a) all consents, including, if applicable, the uses of the CDR data that the CDR consumer has consented to under any use consents; (b) amendments to or withdrawals of consents by CDR consumers; (c) notifications of withdrawals of authorisations received from data holders; (d) CDR complaint data;" ;
    cof:pageNumber "149"^^xsd:integer .

concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-8-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
