    prov:wasDerivedFrom <made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.158" .
doc:sch-4-sec-9-11 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "9 6  Audits by the Commission and the Information Commissioner" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commission may, at any time, audit the compliance of any CDR participant with any or all of the following: (a) Part IVD of the Act, including Division 5 of Part IVD to the extent that it relates to these rules; (b) these rules; (c) the data standards. (2) The Information Commissioner may, at any time, audit the compliance of any CDR participant with any or all of the following: (a) the privacy safeguards (Division 5 of Part IVD of the Act); (b) these rules to the extent that they relate to: (i) the privacy safeguards (see in particular Part 7 of these rules); or (ii) the privacy and confidentiality of CDR data. (3) For the purposes of conducting an audit or otherwise monitoring the compliance of the CDR participant with the provisions mentioned in subrules (1) and (2), the Commission, or the Information Commissioner, may give a CDR participant a written notice that requests the CDR participant to produce, within the time specified in the notice: (a) copies of records that are required by this Division to be kept; or (b) information from such records. (4) The CDR participant must comply with a request under subrule (3). Note: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "158"^^xsd:integer .

