doc:sch-4-sec-9-11-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "9(4) 6  Audits by the Commission and the Information Commissioner" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) The CDR participant must comply with a request under subrule (3). Note: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "158"^^xsd:integer .

concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-12 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "9 7  Audits by the Data Recipient Accreditor"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-9-12 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The CDR Accreditor may, at any time, audit the compliance of an accredited data recipient with any or all of the following: (a) the obligations under rule 5.12; (b) any conditions imposed on their accreditation. (2) For the purposes of conducting an audit or otherwise monitoring the compliance of the accredited data recipient with the criteria and conditions mentioned in subrule (1), the CDR Accreditor may give an accredited data recipient a written notice that requests the accredited data recipient to produce: (a) copies of records that are required by this Division to be kept; or (b) information from such records. (3) The accredited data recipient must comply with a request under subrule (2). Note: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8). (4) The CDR Accreditor must provide a copy of any audit report to the Commission and the Information Commissioner.   Other matters  Part 9 Civil penalty provisions  Division 9.4 Section 9.8 Competition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The CDR Accreditor may, at any time, audit the compliance of an accredited data recipient with any or all of the following: (a) the obligations under rule 5.12; (b) any conditions imposed on their accreditation. (2) For the purposes of conducting an audit or otherwise monitoring the compliance of the accredited data recipient with the criteria and conditions mentioned in subrule (1), the CDR Accreditor may give an accredited data recipient a written notice that requests the accredited data recipient to produce: (a) copies of records that are required by this Division to be kept; or (b) information from such records. (3) The accredited data recipient must comply with a request under subrule (2). Note: This subrule is a civil penalty provision (see rule 9.8). (4) The CDR Accreditor must provide a copy of any audit report to the Commission and the Information Commissioner.   Other matters  Part 9 Civil penalty provisions  Division 9.4 Section 9.8 Competition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "798862ccd52d55c6f1bf75c9276860928dce6a917d4a2329d4dfbc303103fed7" ;
    cof:pageNumber "158"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-12-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-12-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-9-12-ss-3 ;
