concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-6-24 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "6 11  Disclosure of CDR data voluntarily"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-6-24 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A data holder in the banking sector or NBL sector, other than an excluded data holder, may notify the Commission that it wishes Part 2 or Part 4 of these rules to apply to it from a specified date. (2) The data holder, from that specified date, may: (a) receive a request under Part 2 or Part 4 of these rules from a CDR consumer who is eligible in relation to that data holder; and (b) disclose required or voluntary product or consumer data in response to the request. (3) These rules apply to the data holder in respect of that request, and all subsequent requests under Part 2 or Part 4 of these rules by consumers who are eligible in relation to that data holder. Note: This clause means that, among other things, a data holder who elects to receive and respond to such a request must comply with all aspects of these rules relevant to handling it (and all future requests by eligible consumers). For instance, the data holder would need to provide the consumer dashboard in accordance with subrule 1.15(1) upon receiving a request under Part 4, and would need to meet the internal and external dispute resolution requirements.  Schedule 3  Provisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A data holder in the banking sector or NBL sector, other than an excluded data holder, may notify the Commission that it wishes Part 2 or Part 4 of these rules to apply to it from a specified date. (2) The data holder, from that specified date, may: (a) receive a request under Part 2 or Part 4 of these rules from a CDR consumer who is eligible in relation to that data holder; and (b) disclose required or voluntary product or consumer data in response to the request. (3) These rules apply to the data holder in respect of that request, and all subsequent requests under Part 2 or Part 4 of these rules by consumers who are eligible in relation to that data holder. Note: This clause means that, among other things, a data holder who elects to receive and respond to such a request must comply with all aspects of these rules relevant to handling it (and all future requests by eligible consumers). For instance, the data holder would need to provide the consumer dashboard in accordance with subrule 1.15(1) upon receiving a request under Part 4, and would need to meet the internal and external dispute resolution requirements.  Schedule 3  Provisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1e477fda8bfc78b752604af19eb6a440615c1da21e27c3cf4712f7c6ad990d93" ;
    cof:pageNumber "197"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-6-24-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-6-24-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-6-24-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf> ;
    dc:source "made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010.pdf, p.197" .
doc:sch-3-sec-6-24 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "6 11  Disclosure of CDR data voluntarily" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A data holder in the banking sector or NBL sector, other than an excluded data holder, may notify the Commission that it wishes Part 2 or Part 4 of these rules to apply to it from a specified date. (2) The data holder, from that specified date, may: (a) receive a request under Part 2 or Part 4 of these rules from a CDR consumer who is eligible in relation to that data holder; and (b) disclose required or voluntary product or consumer data in response to the request. (3) These rules apply to the data holder in respect of that request, and all subsequent requests under Part 2 or Part 4 of these rules by consumers who are eligible in relation to that data holder. Note: This clause means that, among other things, a data holder who elects to receive and respond to such a request must comply with all aspects of these rules relevant to handling it (and all future requests by eligible consumers). For instance, the data holder would need to provide the consumer dashboard in accordance with subrule 1.15(1) upon receiving a request under Part 4, and would need to meet the internal and external dispute resolution requirements.  Schedule 3  Provisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors" ;
    cof:pageNumber "197"^^xsd:integer .

