doc:sch-3-sec-7-10 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "7 3  Streamlined accreditation—banking sector" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "For paragraph 5.5(b) of these rules, for the banking sector, the criteria for streamlined accreditation are that the accreditation applicant:  Provisions relevant to the banking and non-bank lenders sectors  Schedule 3 Other rules and modifications of these rules, for the banking sector and NBL sector  Part 7 Clause 7.4 Competition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020 (a) is an ADI; but (b) is not a restricted ADI." ;
    cof:pageNumber "200"^^xsd:integer .

concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-3-sec-7-11 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "7 4  Exemptions to accreditation criteria—banking sector"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-7-11 ;
    values:originalText "(1) This clause sets out how the accreditation criteria operate in relation to the banking sector, for the purposes of rule 5.12 of these rules. (2) An accredited person that: (a) is an ADI; but (b) is not a restricted ADI; need not comply with paragraph 5.12(2)(b) of these rules." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This clause sets out how the accreditation criteria operate in relation to the banking sector, for the purposes of rule 5.12 of these rules. (2) An accredited person that: (a) is an ADI; but (b) is not a restricted ADI; need not comply with paragraph 5.12(2)(b) of these rules."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "aa5b36f73c328a1d41d561a583f2d96e981da7325c34326aab1fae5c002e58fc" ;
    cof:pageNumber "201"^^xsd:integer ;
