concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-2-11 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "2 2  Meaning of account privileges—energy sector"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-2-11 ;
    values:originalText "(1) This clause is made for the purposes of the definition of account privileges in subrule 1.7(1) of these rules. (2) For the energy sector, a person has account privileges in relation to an account with a retailer if the person is a customer authorised representative of the account holder for the purposes of: (a) rule 56A of the National Energy Retail Rules; or (b) Chapter 7 of the National Electricity Rules." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This clause is made for the purposes of the definition of account privileges in subrule 1.7(1) of these rules. (2) For the energy sector, a person has account privileges in relation to an account with a retailer if the person is a customer authorised representative of the account holder for the purposes of: (a) rule 56A of the National Energy Retail Rules; or (b) Chapter 7 of the National Electricity Rules."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b3fde3627a3985e732871fe5790e5cfb483843b5839a07324bb3bcd490e2b082" ;
