concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-8-26 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "8 7  Authorisation to disclose CDR data before being required to do so"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-8-26 ;
    values:originalText "(1) This clause applies in relation to a request for disclosure of CDR data that has been made to a retailer in accordance with Part 2, Part 3 or Part 4 of these rules (the relevant data request Part) if: (b) the requested CDR data is any of the following: (i) required product data; (ii) voluntary product data; (iii) required consumer data; (iv) voluntary consumer data; and (c) the requested CDR data includes some pre-application CDR data.  Provisions relevant to the energy sector  Schedule 4 Staged application of these rules to the energy sector  Part 8 Clause 8.7 Competition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020 (2) For these rules, the retailer may disclose any or all of the pre-application CDR data in response to the request in accordance with the relevant data request Part. (3) In this clause, pre-application CDR data means CDR data that, but for the operation of this Part, the data holder would be required or authorised by the relevant data request Part to disclose in response to the request.  Schedule 4  Provisions relevant to the energy sector" ;
    skos:definition "(1) This clause applies in relation to a request for disclosure of CDR data that has been made to a retailer in accordance with Part 2, Part 3 or Part 4 of these rules (the relevant data request Part) if: (b) the requested CDR data is any of the following: (i) required product data; (ii) voluntary product data; (iii) required consumer data; (iv) voluntary consumer data; and (c) the requested CDR data includes some pre-application CDR data.  Provisions relevant to the energy sector  Schedule 4 Staged application of these rules to the energy sector  Part 8 Clause 8.7 Competition and Consumer (Consumer Data Right) Rules 2020 (2) For these rules, the retailer may disclose any or all of the pre-application CDR data in response to the request in accordance with the relevant data request Part. (3) In this clause, pre-application CDR data means CDR data that, but for the operation of this Part, the data holder would be required or authorised by the relevant data request Part to disclose in response to the request.  Schedule 4  Provisions relevant to the energy sector"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ad78a85977a5c90fd0f416f563d5b01dca0128461f84a113fadbf7dcc8933dda" ;
    cof:pageNumber "222"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:made-under-the-competition-and-consumer-act-2010-sch-4-sec-8-26-ss-1 ;
